{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In the morning and HaShem will know those who are His.</b> That is to say: you say that we exalt ourselves over the congregation of HaShem, and that I act on my own initiative — tomorrow you will know this, for in the morning HaShem, may He be exalted, will make known to you those who are His: that is, whether the Levites are His, of whom it written of them (Numbers 8) ״והיו לי הלוים״ — 'and the Levites shall be Mine' — or whether the firstborn are still His, of whom it is written of them (Exodus 13:2) ״קדש לי כל בכור״ — 'sanctify to Me every firstborn' — and who is the holy one, to be High Priest — he is Aaron, of whom it is written (I Chronicles 23:13) ״ויבדל אהרן להקדישו קדש קדשים״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״בקר ויודע ה׳ את אשר לו״ — R. Nathan said: The Holy One, blessed be He, said: If all the sorcerers of the world gather together, they cannot turn morning into evening; and just as I separated between light and darkness, so did I separate Aaron to sanctify him holy of holies."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:55.884625311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}